{"book":"PSA","chapter":43,"source":"hbo","verses":[1,2,3,4,5],"records":[{"id":"PSA.43.1.s1","verses":[1],"source":"שָׁפְטֵ֤נִי אֱלֹהִ֨ים׀וְרִ֘יבָ֤ה רִיבִ֗י מִגּ֥וֹי לֹא־חָסִ֑יד מֵ֤אִישׁ־מִרְמָ֖ה וְעַוְלָ֣ה תְפַלְּטֵֽנִי׃","gloss":"Judge me, God, and plead my case against a nation not faithful; from a man of deceit and injustice rescue me.","pieces":[[1,"Give judgment for me, God, and take up my case against a nation without loyalty; save me from people who lie and do wrong.",null]],"L":{"1":"Judge me, God, and plead my case against a nation not faithful; from the {{gender:person|man}} of deceit and injustice rescue me."},"R":{"1":"God, show that I am right. Defend me against people who are not loyal to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}. Save me from people who lie and are unfair."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o190430010011"],"choice":"Psalm 43 continues Psalm 42","alternatives":[],"reason":"This psalm has no title and shares the refrain of Psalm 42 (verse 5; 42:6, 12), so it is the last part of the same poem. Here the complaint turns to prayer.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190430010011","o190430010032","o190430010041"],"choice":"judge me, plead my case: take my side in court","alternatives":[],"reason":"He asks God to act as judge and as his advocate, and so to clear him (7:9; 26:1; 35:1).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190430010071"],"choice":"not faithful: without loyal love","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (chasid) is the one of 4:4; a nation without it keeps no faith with God or others.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["L"],"category":"setting_alternative","tokens":["o190430010082"],"choice":"person, with \"man\" as the alternative","alternatives":[],"reason":"The phrase is general: anyone deceitful and unjust.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-2","layer":"rendering","levels":["B","R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190430010082"],"choice":"people (plural)","alternatives":["the man"],"reason":"Balanced and Readable speak of such people as a group.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-3","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o190430010071"],"choice":"to you","alternatives":[],"reason":"Readable says to whom they are not loyal (m3).","uncertain":true,"footnote":false}],"heading":"Send out your light and truth","status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.43.2.s1","verses":[2],"source":"כִּֽי־אַתָּ֤ה׀אֱלֹהֵ֣י מָֽעוּזִּי֮ לָמָ֪ה זְנַ֫חְתָּ֥נִי לָֽמָּה־קֹדֵ֥ר אֶתְהַלֵּ֗ךְ בְּלַ֣חַץ אוֹיֵֽב׃","gloss":"For you [are the] God of my stronghold; why have you rejected me? Why mourning do I go about in [the] oppression of an enemy?","pieces":[[2,"For {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} are God, my fortress. Why have {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} pushed me away? Why do I walk about dressed in grief while the enemy presses me hard?",null]],"L":{"2":"For {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} [are] the God of my stronghold; why have {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} rejected me? Why do I walk about mourning under the oppression of an enemy?"},"R":{"2":"You are God, and {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} keep me safe. So why have {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} turned me away? Why am I so sad? Why do my enemies treat me so badly?"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190430020041"],"choice":"my stronghold: my place of refuge","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (ma'oz) is a fortress, a strong place to flee to (27:1; 31:5).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o190430020072","o190430020111"],"choice":"42:10 repeated","alternatives":[],"reason":"The question repeats 42:10, with \"rejected\" in place of \"forgotten\". The same wording is used at each level.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190430020061"],"choice":"rejected: pushed away","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verb (zanach) is to cast off or spurn (44:10, 24).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.43.3.s1","verses":[3],"source":"שְׁלַח־אוֹרְךָ֣ וַ֭אֲמִתְּךָ הֵ֣מָּה יַנְח֑וּנִי יְבִיא֥וּנִי אֶל־הַֽר־קָ֝דְשְׁךָ֗ וְאֶל־מִשְׁכְּנוֹתֶֽיךָ׃","gloss":"Send your light and your truth; they will lead me; they will bring me to [the] mountain of your holiness and to your dwellings.","pieces":[[3,"Let {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} light and {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} truth go out to guide me; may they lead me up to {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} holy mountain, to the place where {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} live.",null]],"L":{"3":"Send out {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} light and {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} truth; let them lead me; let them bring me to {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} holy mountain and to {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} dwelling places."},"R":{"3":"Send {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} light and {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} truth to show me the way. Let them lead me back to {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} holy mountain, to the place where {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} live."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o190430030021","o190430030032"],"choice":"your light and your truth: God's guides sent ahead","alternatives":[],"reason":"Light and truth are pictured as two messengers God sends to bring the exile home, as his loyal love goes out in 42:9 (compare 57:4).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o190430030081","o190430030091"],"choice":"your holy mountain: Zion, where the temple stood","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 2:6 and 3:5. This answers the longing of 42:3.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190430030111"],"choice":"your dwellings: God's house","alternatives":[],"reason":"The plural (mishkenot) is the dwelling of God, the sanctuary (84:2).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o190430030051"],"choice":"back","alternatives":[],"reason":"Readable makes clear that he is returning (42:5).","uncertain":true,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.43.4.s1","verses":[4],"source":"וְאָב֤וֹאָה׀אֶל־מִזְבַּ֬ח אֱלֹהִ֗ים אֶל־אֵל֮ שִׂמְחַ֪ת גִּ֫ילִ֥י וְאוֹדְךָ֥ בְכִנּ֗וֹר אֱלֹהִ֥ים אֱלֹהָֽי׃","gloss":"And I will come to [the] altar of God, to God, [the] joy of my rejoicing, and I will give thanks to you with [the] lyre, God, my God.","pieces":[[4,"Then I will come up to God's altar, to God, who is my gladness and my joy, and with the lyre I will give {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} thanks, God, my God.",null]],"L":{"4":"And I will come to the altar of God, to God, the joy of my rejoicing, and I will give thanks to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} with [the] lyre, God, my God."},"R":{"4":"Then I will go to God's altar. God makes me so very happy! I will play the harp and thank {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}, God, my God."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o190430040071","o190430040081"],"choice":"the joy of my rejoicing: my greatest joy","alternatives":[],"reason":"Two words for joy are joined to say that God is his joy above all.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o190430040102"],"choice":"the lyre: a small stringed instrument","alternatives":[],"reason":"The kinnor was a hand-held lyre, played to accompany songs of praise (33:2).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190430040102"],"choice":"harp","alternatives":["lyre"],"reason":"Readable uses the better-known word for a stringed instrument plucked by hand.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.43.5.s1","verses":[5],"source":"מַה־תִּשְׁתּ֬וֹחֲחִ֨י׀נַפְשִׁי֮ וּֽמַה־תֶּהֱמִ֪י עָ֫לָ֥י הוֹחִ֣ילִי לֵֽ֭אלֹהִים כִּי־ע֣וֹד אוֹדֶ֑נּוּ יְשׁוּעֹ֥ת פָּ֝נַ֗י וֵֽאלֹהָֽי׃","gloss":"Why are you bowed down, my soul, and why are you in turmoil within me? Wait for God, for I will yet give thanks to him, [the] salvation of my face and my God.","pieces":[[5,"Why are you bent so low, my soul? Why this unrest inside me? Wait for God in hope; I will give {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} thanks again, the one who saves me, my God.",null]],"L":{"5":"Why are you bowed down, my soul, and why are you in turmoil within me? Wait for God, for I will yet give thanks to {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}, the salvation of my face and my God."},"R":{"5":"I tell myself: Why are you so sad? Why are you so upset? Keep hoping in God! I will praise {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} again. He saves me. He is my God."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o190430050031"],"choice":"my soul: the psalmist speaks to himself","alternatives":[],"reason":"The refrain is a conversation inside the psalmist: one part of him asks why his soul is so low and urges it to hope. Soul (nefesh) is the whole self, here his own heart.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190430050021","o190430050051"],"choice":"bowed down, in turmoil: crushed and restless","alternatives":[],"reason":"The first verb (shachach) is to be bent low, sunk down; the second (hamah) is the roaring or restlessness of the sea, which the poem pictures in 42:8.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o190430050121","o190430050131"],"choice":"the salvation of my face: the one who saves me in person","alternatives":["the help of my countenance"],"reason":"The plural \"salvations\" (yeshu'ot) means full rescue. \"My face\" stands for the person: God is the one who saves him and lifts his face again.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190430050031"],"choice":"I tell myself: Why are you ...","alternatives":["Why are you ..., my soul?"],"reason":"Readable makes clear that he is speaking to himself (m1).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m4","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o190430050142"],"choice":"the refrain closes the poem","alternatives":[],"reason":"The same words as 42:12. The third refrain now follows a prayer and a vow of praise (verses 3-4), so its hope sounds stronger.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"}],"words":{"1":[{"id":"o190430010011","text":"שָׁפְטֵ֤","after":"","lemma":"שָׁפַט","morph":"Vqv2ms","gloss":"vindicate","strong":"8199","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Qal · imperative · 2nd person masculine singular"},{"id":"o190430010012","text":"נִי","after":" ","lemma":"הוּא","morph":"Sp1cs","gloss":"me","strong":"5204a","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Suffix · pronoun · 1st person common singular"},{"id":"o190430010021","text":"אֱלֹהִ֨ים","after":"׀","lemma":"אֱלֹהִים","morph":"Ncmpa","gloss":"O.God","strong":"0430","transliteration":"ʾĕlōhiym","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine plural absolute"},{"id":"o190430010031","text":"וְ","after":"","lemma":"וְ","morph":"C","gloss":"and","strong":"2050b","transliteration":"wə","lang":"H","parse":"Conjunction"},{"id":"o190430010032","text":"רִ֘יבָ֤","after":"","lemma":"רִיב","morph":"Vqv2ms","gloss":"conduct","strong":"7378","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Qal · imperative · 2nd person masculine singular"},{"id":"o190430010033","text":"ה","after":" ","lemma":"ה","morph